# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# The gRPC library at /usr/local/grpc is not built with TSan, so its internal
# synchronization (completion queues, call combiners) is invisible to the
# sanitizer and everything flowing through it is reported as a race.  Suppress
# reports with gRPC frames in them.
#
# CAUTION: our reactor code (asyncWriter.cppm) runs on gRPC callback threads,
# so real races there can carry grpc:: frames and be hidden by these entries.
# For a fully rigorous run, rebuild gRPC itself with -fsanitize=thread and
# delete this file.  Patterns are anchored globs: trailing * is required to
# match a name prefix.
race:grpc_core::*
race:grpc::*
race:grpc_*
race:*cq_end_op_for_callback*
